|description={{et|1=Vesikirp perekonnast Kiivrik (''Daphnia'') pildistatud mikroskoobi all kasutades 8x objektiivi. Isend on kogutud 2023. aasta 9. juulil. Pildil on eriti huvipakkuv seljapoolses haudetaskus paiknev tume püsimuna ehk ephippium - see on spetsiaalne vastupidav struktuur, mis tekib ebasoodsate keskkonnatingimuste saabudes. Püsimuna tootmine on vesikirpude ellujäämisstrateegia, võimaldades neil ebasoodsad tingimused üle elada, sarnaselt taimede seemnetega. Looma läbipaistvas kehas on näha ka omapärane võrkjas muster ning sinakad värvitoonid.
Pilt on tehtud musta tausta peal, mis toob esile looma läbipaistva kehakatte ja selles paikneva tumeda püsimuna. Valgustamisel on kasutatud peegelduvat valgust fotograafia välklambilt (''speedlight''), mis rõhutab eriti hästi isendi välispinna struktuure. Pilt on tehtud kasutades fookuse virnastamise tehnikat (''focus stacking''), mis tagab suure teravussügavuse.}}
{{en|1=A water flea of genus Daphnia photographed under a microscope using an 8x objective. The specimen was collected on July 9, 2023. Of particular interest is the dark resting egg or ephippium in the dorsal brood pouch - this is a specialized resistant structure that forms when environmental conditions become unfavorable. The production of resting eggs is a survival strategy of water fleas, allowing them to survive adverse conditions, similar to plant seeds. The transparent body also shows a characteristic reticulated pattern and bluish tints.
The specimen was photographed against a black background, which highlights the transparent carapace and the dark resting egg within. The lighting technique used was reflected light from a photographic speedlight flash, which particularly emphasizes the surface structures. The image was created using focus stacking technique, which ensures great depth of field throughout the subject.}}
